  "searchTokens": "Feature Scaling Interactive Jupyter notebook covering Feature Scaling. Contains 13 executable code cells and 0 explanation sections. feature engineering feature scaling normalization standardization import pandas as pd df = pd.read_csv('SampleFile.csv') df.head() df.info() import numpy as np\nmax_vals = np.max(np.abs(df))\nmax_vals print((df - max_vals) / max_vals) #MinMax Scaling from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler\n\nscaler = MinMaxScaler()\nscaled_data = scaler.fit_transform(df)\nscaled_df = pd.DataFrame(scaled_data, \n                         columns=df.columns)\nscaled_df.head() #Normalisation\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import Normalizer\n\nscaler = Normalizer()\nscaled_data = scaler.fit_transform(df)\nscaled_df = pd.DataFrame(scaled_data,\n                         columns=df.columns)\nprint(scaled_df.head()) #Standarisation\n\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n\nscaler = StandardScaler()\nscaled_data = scaler.fit_transform(df)\nscaled_df = pd.DataFrame(scaled_data,\n                         columns=df.columns)\nprint(scaled_df.head())",
